      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auth): bind OAuth and sessions to immutable identity",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nHarden the two GitHub authentication identity boundaries:\n\n- bind portal OAuth callbacks to the browser that initiated login\n- bind signed sessions and durable ownership to GitHub's immutable numeric account ID\n\n## Changes\n\n- issue a short-lived `__Host-crabbox_oauth` cookie and retain only its SHA-256 hash\n- validate the browser binding before exchanging the authorization code\n- clear the binding after terminal portal outcomes\n- use `github:<numeric-id>` as the authenticated owner identity\n- re-fetch `/user` during membership revalidation and require its account ID to match the session owner\n- reject legacy email-owned sessions instead of automatically transferring access to the current holder of that email\n- preserve verified email checks and the existing CLI OAuth confirmation flow\n\n## Compatibility\n\nExisting GitHub sessions or durable records owned by an email fail closed for non-admin access and require explicit migration or recreation. No email-to-account ownership transfer is performed automatically.\n\nAdministrators should use immutable `github:<numeric-id>` values in `CRABBOX_GITHUB_ADMIN_OWNERS`; the existing login allowlist remains supported for compatibility.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded focused regression coverage for:\n\n- missing or incorrect portal browser binding\n- successful one-time callback and cookie cleanup\n- callback replay\n- immutable account ID revalidation\n- account ID mismatch\n- rejection of legacy email-owned sessions\n- organization, team, and revocation checks\n\nFull repository CI is pending on this draft PR.",
        "branch": "agent/oauth-browser-binding",
